    {
      "hotel": {
        "id": "H0375",
        "content": {
          "name": "Burj Al Arab",
          "virginView": "This instantly recognisable iconic building rising from the Arabian Gulf attracts international attention and awe, making it one of the most photographed buildings in the world! It is also one of the most luxurious offering sumptuous all suite accommodations with stunning views of the Arabian Gulf. Each floor has its own private reception desk and a brigade of highly trained butlers, ensuring guests enjoy the ultimate in personal service. A trip to Talise Spa and Fitness is essential. Sublime treatments, tailor-made to suit your personal needs, will chase everyday cares away. There&#x2019;s also sauna and steam rooms, a cold plunge pool, an infinity pool and a state-of-the-art gym to keep the body beautiful. If you have children, you can still enjoy all amenities to the full thanks to Kids' Club at Jumeirah Al Naseem or Jumeirah Al Qasr. When it comes to dining, there are six award-winning restaurants to choose from including Al Iwan in the heart of the world&#x2019;s tallest atrium, flanked by golden columns and serving the finest Arabian cuisine. Al Muntaha sits 200 metres above sea level and Sahn Eddar serves afternoon tea. When the sun goes down, the pace picks up at Skyview Bar, adjacent to Al Muntaha and one of the places to be seen in Dubai and your stay wouldn't be complete if you didn't visit the elegant GILT bar, known for being entirely decorated in gold decor, it's creative cocktail menu and beautiful views over the city.",
          "telephoneBookableOnly": false,
          "vRating": "5+",
          "hotelDescription": "This is simply the ultimate in hedonistic living and is the place to be and the place to be seen.You haven&#x2019;t truly experienced decadence until you&#x2019;ve been to Dubai and thanks to a series of jaw-dropping luxuries such as: a fleet of Rolls Royce cars, butlers available around-the-clock and reception desks on every floor, the Burj Al Arab certainly lives up to every superlative going.In discerning company it is referred to as the most luxurious resort in the world and as rooms are incredibly spacious (they are huge!) and contain some fabulous fixtures and fittings, it&#x2019;s not hard to see why.The six restaurants are just as magnificent as the rooms and with chances to dine in the world&#x2019;s tallest atrium, in front of an aquarium and suspended 200 metres above sea level, you won&#x2019;t forget Dubai in a hurry!",
          "atAGlance": [
            "Unparalleled luxury with suite-only accommodation",
            "5 swimming pools and private beach",
            "Personalised butler service",
            "9 signature restaurants and bars"
          ],
          "location": {
            "lat": 25.141088,
            "lon": 55.18527
          },
          "parentLocation": "Dubai Beach, Dubai",
